Players Analysis Page
Overview & Purpose
This dashboard examines individual player contributions, team-level goal reliance, and the statistical distribution of goals among goalscorers.

Key Insights
Broad Participation: A total of 308 goals were scored across the tournament by 182 distinct goalscorers.

Goal Distribution Curve: The vast majority of goalscorers (127 players) scored a single goal. Only an elite group of 10 players managed to score 4 or more goals.

Duo-Driven Attack: France led total team contributions with 16 goals—heavily driven by Mbappé (10) and Dembélé (6). Similarly, Argentina relied on Messi (8) and Julián Álvarez (4) for 12 of their total goals.
